{
  "note": [
    "The per-package coverage floors. Written by `tools/covercheck -write-baseline` from a real run, and read by the same tool as a gate.",
    "",
    "These are floors, not targets. A package below its floor fails the build. A package above its floor plus the margin also fails, and asks for the floor to be raised — a floor that only fails downwards is a floor somebody lowers once and everything above it is free afterwards.",
    "",
    "They are statement coverage from `go test -coverprofile`, not branch coverage: `go test` does not produce branch coverage, and a metric this repository cannot measure with a flag is a metric it reports without measuring.",
    "",
    "The floors hold for the build modes in `build`. Coverage is not a property of the source: internal/migrate measures 78.6% without -race and 71.4% with it on an unchanged tree, so a floor from one mode is not a floor for the other, and `check` reports that it could not measure rather than comparing numbers that do not belong together.",
    "",
    "`cmd/`, `migrations/` and `tools/` are named in `excluded` and are not floored. `migrations` is SQL with a Python harness beside it and no Go statements, and a floor of zero for a directory with no code teaches a reader to ignore this file."
  ],
